  "_meta": {
    "source": "https://www.tesla.com/api/energy/supercharger/pricing?countryCode={CC}&productType=SuperCharger&stateCode={SC}",
    "harvested": "2026-06-04",
    "method": "same-origin fetch from logged-in browser console (Akamai-gated; automation/curl get 403)",
    "notes": [
      "31 markets returned live pricing; almost entirely Europe + UAE/Israel/Turkey.",
      "Non-US countries return IDENTICAL pricing across every region tested -> national rates. US is the only per-state country.",
      "HTTP 500 = country recognized but no pricing configured (treated as NOT live).",
      "Press-list Saudi/Qatar/Jordan all return 500 -> not actually serving pricing. Germany & the Nordics ARE live despite no press mention.",
      "ANOMALY: US cabinet hardware ($55k) is ~60% higher than the ~$34k-equivalent everywhere else.",
      "ANOMALY: Norway cabinet (39,300 NOK ~= EUR3.4k) is ~10x too low vs the EUR33k baseline; energy/sell/fee scale correctly. Likely a Tesla data bug (Maine-style). Do not trust NO hardware until reverified.",
      "ANOMALY: US Maine still returns raw 0.008 energy cost -> keep the 0.15 override.",
      "Most non-US records below are the compact discovery sample (cur,e,p,u,fee,cabinet). Full hardware/install breakdown captured only for US/DE/FR/ES/IT/AE; a follow-up full-record pull is pending for the rest."
    ],
    "fields": {
      "e": "averageEnergyCost (utility cost to host, native ccy/kWh)",
      "p": "scMedianPriceToEVDriver (sell price, native ccy/kWh)",
      "u": "scAvgUtilization (kWh per stall per day)",
      "fee": "scTeslaFeePPU (Tesla all-inclusive fee, native ccy/kWh)",
      "cabinet": "scCabinetCost (per stall, native ccy)",
      "hardwarePerStall": "cabinet+otherHardware+services+shipping (full records only)"
    },
    "note_2026_06_13": "Refreshed: Maine energy 0.008->0.293 (Tesla fixed). See sfb-pricing-full.json for intl sell-price + Norway hardware corrections.",
    "note_2026_08_01": "Aug 1 re-verify: all 51 usStates below re-fetched and IDENTICAL (no drift since Jun 13); Maine holds at 0.293 so the 0.15 override is no longer needed. Swept all 249 ISO alpha-2 codes: 31 non-US markets priced (LI/Liechtenstein is new to this archive and was never tested before), 217 return 500, US requires a stateCode. Key API semantics: stateCode is validated for US ONLY - outside the US it is ignored (bogus/empty/omitted all return the same national record), so a 500 is always 'market not configured', never a bad region code. Public pages: 28 of 32 markets now live, up from 11."
  },
